<onlyinclude>'''Intersubjectivity''' concerns relations between subjects through which experiences, meanings or aspects of a shared world become mutually intelligible. It appears in phenomenology, social theory and research on interaction.

== Explanation ==
Two people can coordinate attention to the same object and discuss it even if their individual experiences differ. Conversation allows them to identify and repair misunderstandings. Shared understanding does not require identical minds or guarantee that their shared belief is true.

